1
00:00:41,066 --> 00:00:42,066
Whoa!

2
00:00:42,733 --> 00:00:44,033
You're painting blind!

3
00:00:44,466 --> 00:00:45,466
Impressive!

4
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:46,500
Respect!

5
00:00:55,466 --> 00:00:56,500
You okay?

6
00:01:01,866 --> 00:01:03,700
I shouldn't have gone in that room.

7
00:01:04,666 --> 00:01:05,866
It won't happen again.

8
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:11,200
Mm.

9
00:01:11,666 --> 00:01:13,700
I accept your apology.

10
00:01:15,866 --> 00:01:17,632
Since you accept my apology

11
00:01:17,633 --> 00:01:18,900
then don't look so unhappy.

12
00:01:18,933 --> 00:01:19,933
Come on.

13
00:01:20,233 --> 00:01:23,533
Can you quit that habit of
putting your hands on me?

14
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:29,300
And what's that smell on you?

15
00:01:29,466 --> 00:01:30,466
Huh?

16
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:32,000
Ah.

17
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:33,400
Cooking grease.

18
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:35,233
I learned to cook from Yong Qi.

19
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:37,300
You think

20
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:38,866
looking after someone is easy?

21
00:01:39,133 --> 00:01:40,800
I never asked you to learn.

22
00:01:42,876 --> 00:01:45,700
Getting stuck with a boss
like you... unbelievable.

23
00:01:46,413 --> 00:01:48,346
Ugh, can you go shower first?

24
00:01:48,390 --> 00:01:49,957
The smell is really strong.

25
00:01:50,666 --> 00:01:52,900
But I like this smell of real life.

26
00:01:53,179 --> 00:01:54,259
Feels like all of a sudden.

27
00:01:54,866 --> 00:01:56,533
I'm back in the mortal world.

28
00:01:57,066 --> 00:01:59,365
Then hurry back up to your heaven.

29
00:01:59,366 --> 00:02:00,566
They need you there more.

30
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:07,533
So you don't need me?

31
00:02:13,180 --> 00:02:13,446
Hey.

32
00:02:13,966 --> 00:02:14,966
What are you doing?

33
00:02:15,033 --> 00:02:16,033
What are you doing?

34
00:02:16,175 --> 00:02:17,642
It's a perfectly good painting,

35
00:02:17,666 --> 00:02:18,666
why toss it?

36
00:02:20,266 --> 00:02:21,466
What's good about it?

37
00:02:22,066 --> 00:02:24,000
It's just emotional scribbles.

38
00:02:24,433 --> 00:02:25,866
I think it's good.

39
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:27,833
And you painted it blind.

40
00:02:27,866 --> 00:02:29,933
Who knows,
it could sell for a lot!

41
00:02:32,300 --> 00:02:33,533
You know art?

42
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:36,566
I know money.

43
00:02:37,533 --> 00:02:39,166
Even if no gallery takes it

44
00:02:39,266 --> 00:02:40,900
you can at least sell it online.

45
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:42,700
And then

46
00:02:42,766 --> 00:02:43,766
we go fifty-fifty.

47
00:02:44,900 --> 00:02:47,433
You don't have to keep
finding ways to flatter me.

48
00:02:48,266 --> 00:02:49,600
I'm not falling for that.

49
00:02:50,933 --> 00:02:55,833
Xu Feiyu, you're questioning
the eye of a business genius.

50
00:02:58,233 --> 00:03:00,733
A top student at the National
University of Singapore

51
00:03:01,633 --> 00:03:03,300
sure knows how to suck up.

52
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:43,933
If we were in Singapore

53
00:03:44,833 --> 00:03:45,833
your paintings

54
00:03:46,566 --> 00:03:48,366
would hang in the best spot in Ginza. [TN:
Continuity error, "Ginza" isn't in Singapore]

55
00:05:29,933 --> 00:05:31,799
Quit it.

56
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:32,066
Hmm.

57
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:33,266
Song Yi.

58
00:05:33,966 --> 00:05:34,600
What is it?

59
00:05:34,601 --> 00:05:36,833
Quit it, aah! Aah.

60
00:05:36,966 --> 00:05:39,032
Song Yi! What are you...!

61
00:05:39,033 --> 00:05:41,533
Aah.

62
00:05:43,466 --> 00:05:44,433
Okay, okay, okay!

63
00:05:44,433 --> 00:05:45,433
Stop, stop, stop!

64
00:05:45,466 --> 00:05:46,965
Now you want to stop?

65
00:05:46,966 --> 00:05:47,966
No way!

66
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:51,799
All right, all right

67
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:52,800
I give up! I give up!

68
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:55,300
Hey! Don't get water in my eyes.

69
00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:00,900
My clothes are soaked.

70
00:06:02,093 --> 00:06:04,500
Well then
do you want to get in with me?

71
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:07,500
Is that okay?

72
00:06:08,966 --> 00:06:09,966
Mm.

73
00:06:10,266 --> 00:06:11,266
Sure...

74
00:06:12,500 --> 00:06:13,066
All right then

75
00:06:13,266 --> 00:06:14,266
here I come.

76
00:06:59,200 --> 00:07:00,566
The air's so good.

77
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:03,199
So many orioles around here.

78
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:04,166
Yeah.

79
00:07:04,166 --> 00:07:05,166
They sound lovely.

80
00:07:05,300 --> 00:07:06,300
Wow.

81
00:07:12,266 --> 00:07:13,266
Wow.

82
00:07:24,366 --> 00:07:25,366
Song Yi

83
00:07:25,533 --> 00:07:26,533
feel this too.

84
00:08:04,433 --> 00:08:05,433
Careful, go slow.

85
00:08:26,333 --> 00:08:27,366
Xu Feiyu

86
00:08:28,666 --> 00:08:29,900
does anyone live here?

87
00:08:31,066 --> 00:08:32,066
No.

88
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:33,832
Don't tell me this is...

89
00:08:33,833 --> 00:08:34,833
This place

90
00:08:35,033 --> 00:08:37,233
was my dad's old art studio.

91
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:39,600
But

92
00:08:39,833 --> 00:08:42,533
now it's just an empty house.

93
00:08:57,133 --> 00:08:58,266
It's so clean in here.

94
00:08:59,133 --> 00:09:00,333
You keep it up yourself?

95
00:09:01,400 --> 00:09:02,600
Yong Qi does.

96
00:09:03,733 --> 00:09:05,400
She comes to clean it regularly.

97
00:09:06,500 --> 00:09:07,600
Yong Qi?

98
00:09:08,433 --> 00:09:10,866
Didn't think she'd be that reliable.

99
00:09:11,800 --> 00:09:12,366
Nice.

100
00:09:12,733 --> 00:09:13,766
She's done a good job.

101
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:15,500
Saves me cleaning it myself.

102
00:10:02,733 --> 00:10:04,065
Your eyes aren't healed yet.

103
00:10:04,066 --> 00:10:05,066
You can't drink.

104
00:10:05,400 --> 00:10:07,333
Just for today.

105
00:10:09,366 --> 00:10:10,066
Fine.

106
00:10:10,300 --> 00:10:11,600
Wouldn't say no.

107
00:10:12,433 --> 00:10:14,266
Drinking alone's no fun anyway.

108
00:10:36,033 --> 00:10:37,039
Xu Feiyu.

109
00:10:37,063 --> 00:10:37,596
Hm?

110
00:10:37,834 --> 00:10:40,066
Did you use to come here alone a lot?

111
00:10:41,633 --> 00:10:43,366
I came here a lot as a kid.

112
00:10:43,913 --> 00:10:45,313
As a kid?

113
00:10:45,792 --> 00:10:47,425
Tell me, I want to hear.

114
00:10:48,100 --> 00:10:49,766
There's nothing to tell.

115
00:10:50,033 --> 00:10:52,032
Come on, tell me.

116
00:10:52,033 --> 00:10:53,700
There's got to be something fun.

117
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:02,833
When I was a kid

118
00:11:03,166 --> 00:11:05,833
a lot of artists built studios around here.

119
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:08,899
So this place used to be

120
00:11:08,900 --> 00:11:11,066
some kind of artists' colony.

121
00:11:12,666 --> 00:11:14,266
This house...

122
00:11:14,533 --> 00:11:17,066
my dad built it with his own hands.

123
00:11:18,266 --> 00:11:20,066
I remember at night

124
00:11:20,166 --> 00:11:22,033
a lot of small animals would come in.

125
00:11:22,900 --> 00:11:24,132
One time

126
00:11:24,133 --> 00:11:25,532
a wild boar got in

127
00:11:25,533 --> 00:11:27,366
and ruined several of his paintings.

128
00:11:29,333 --> 00:11:30,633
After that

129
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:33,500
he'd light a fire in the stove at night

130
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:36,233
and the boar never came back.

131
00:11:41,133 --> 00:11:42,600
So do you miss him?

132
00:11:49,633 --> 00:11:50,866
Today

133
00:11:51,633 --> 00:11:53,066
is his birthday.

134
00:11:53,833 --> 00:11:54,200
Tch.

135
00:11:54,466 --> 00:11:57,100
Birthday? Almost forgot.

136
00:11:57,700 --> 00:11:59,000
What did you say?

137
00:12:00,066 --> 00:12:01,066
Ah.

138
00:12:01,433 --> 00:12:02,500
Nothing.

139
00:12:02,733 --> 00:12:04,265
What I mean is…

140
00:12:04,266 --> 00:12:05,665
we should both wish him

141
00:12:05,666 --> 00:12:06,700
a happy birthday.

142
00:12:06,732 --> 00:12:07,732
Cheers.

143
00:12:08,666 --> 00:12:10,966
But I never wanted him to be happy.

144
00:12:15,233 --> 00:12:16,599
What I wanted

145
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:19,133
was that he'd pick an unhappy family

146
00:12:20,133 --> 00:12:22,333
living in a filthy, run-down house

147
00:12:23,866 --> 00:12:27,933
and rats... so many rats.

148
00:12:31,933 --> 00:12:32,933
Oh right.

149
00:12:33,466 --> 00:12:35,166
And send him a few wild boars.

150
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:38,566
But

151
00:12:38,866 --> 00:12:41,033
I heard he has a happy family

152
00:12:41,133 --> 00:12:42,666
and a son too.

153
00:12:43,733 --> 00:12:44,866
I think

154
00:12:46,100 --> 00:12:47,499
that son...

155
00:12:47,500 --> 00:12:49,700
must be a better son than me.

156
00:12:59,633 --> 00:13:01,466
So why did he walk out?

157
00:13:08,833 --> 00:13:10,500
The year I was eleven.

158
00:13:12,200 --> 00:13:14,133
I remember it was his birthday too.

159
00:13:15,533 --> 00:13:18,166
I found a rat in my room.

160
00:13:19,866 --> 00:13:21,165
Because of that rat

161
00:13:21,166 --> 00:13:22,899
he tore the whole place apart

162
00:13:22,900 --> 00:13:24,733
and got in a fight with Mom.

163
00:13:26,666 --> 00:13:27,933
Then...

164
00:13:31,046 --> 00:13:32,246
Then...

165
00:13:33,066 --> 00:13:36,266
he said he'd go down to
the convenience store for a rat trap

166
00:13:37,933 --> 00:13:39,766
and he never came back.

167
00:13:41,066 --> 00:13:43,133
He just made an excuse and ran?

168
00:13:43,933 --> 00:13:45,800
That's beyond irresponsible.

169
00:13:46,733 --> 00:13:49,533
If I hadn't found that rat

170
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:52,866
maybe none of it would have happened.

171
00:13:55,600 --> 00:13:56,700
Xu Feiyu

172
00:13:57,800 --> 00:14:00,433
don't blame yourself for everything.

173
00:14:00,900 --> 00:14:02,700
It was just a rat.

174
00:14:02,866 --> 00:14:04,432
It couldn't change anything.

175
00:14:04,433 --> 00:14:06,033
It's over now.

176
00:14:06,866 --> 00:14:08,333
You're grown up now.

177
00:14:09,066 --> 00:14:10,566
Forget about that rat.

178
00:14:15,633 --> 00:14:17,766
He just left without a word.

179
00:14:19,866 --> 00:14:21,933
I don't even know where he went.

180
00:14:36,133 --> 00:14:37,332
Then today

181
00:14:37,333 --> 00:14:39,133
I'll let you drink a little more.

182
00:14:39,286 --> 00:14:40,286
Hm?

183
00:15:06,100 --> 00:15:07,133
I'll go have a smoke.

184
00:15:08,066 --> 00:15:09,066
I'll be right outside.

185
00:15:09,600 --> 00:15:12,366
If you need anything,
just call me.

186
00:15:13,866 --> 00:15:14,866
Okay.
